  <uml:Package xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499781608893_736279_36119" xmi:uuid="219224ab-e3c7-42e8-8fc1-e0e408f1059e" xmi:type="uml:Package">
    <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_8e001ed_1510147733373_764707_30999" xmi:uuid="fb4c92fe-6d8a-4953-a849-85f8970f8981" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
      <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499781608893_736279_36119"/>
      <body>This capability represents common information to be used such as:&lt;br&gt; the identification of product or activity data. &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;It allows for the identification of classes: &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Identifiers can be defined and put into hierarchical relationships, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Classification information can be assigned to identifiers. This capability enables the description of product or activity data. It allows for the description of classes, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Descriptors can be defined and put into hierarchical relationships, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Classification information can be assigned to descriptors.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; the classification of product or activity data: &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt; it allows for the identification of classes, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;classes can be defined in a class system and put into hierarchical relationships, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Classification information can be assigned to product or activity data, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;the association of classes and product data can be characterized by property definitions.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; The date and time: &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;a date and time can be used in combination with persons and organizations or directly associated with product data, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;a date and time information consists of simple calendar dates or time stamps more complex definitions like spans of time or events.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; The specification of properties and their association with other product data like parts or documents: &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;a property is the definition of a special quality and may reflect physics or arbitrary, user defined measurements, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;a general pattern for instantiating property information is defined by this capability, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;properties can exist independently from their association with product or activity data, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;properties are defined globally and have a value associated, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;independent properties may be assigned to product data, &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;for simple use cases, which do not require the full property concept, a simple property mechanism is provided. This allows for the association of a name value pair with product data.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; The figure below provides an overview of the capability. &lt;figure&gt;&lt;name&gt;CommonResources_domainModel_Overview.png&lt;/name&gt;Simplified overview of the AP242 common resources Domain model&lt;/figure&gt;</body>
    </ownedComment>
    <name>CommonResources</name>
