        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_271a0567_1524672009016_931009_83407"/>
        <body>The parametric properties are the same than the ones used in the other alternative parametric diagram.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1455719447765_491538_43035" xmi:uuid="ec03f95a-0a73-47bb-b94d-cbb0c31a61e8" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193085_795041_23538"/>
        <body>An EffectivityAssignment is an object that associates an Effectivity with the product or activity data whose effectivity is controlled by the associated Effectivity. The association of an Effectivity to product or activity data does not imply any statement concerning effectivity outside of the specified interval. The same applies in the absence of any AssignedEffectivity, that is, no statement concerning effectivity is implied.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>EffectivityAssignment</name>
