    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193149_135029_23667" xmi:uuid="6246459e-c43c-4d83-8c43-0951cae0ec9b" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_290014c_1515863908546_231744_73582" xmi:uuid="563b4c5a-49c7-4ffd-9b8a-49c0f10798de" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193838_333323_27812"/>
        <body>The one and only Domain object using ValidityContextSelect is ModelPropertyAssignment, which maps to Applied_independent_property. Considering this select's members, only ARM Classification_assignment object will handle the mapping paths.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1455695730108_656155_42435" xmi:uuid="76e9fdf1-4868-4f7d-b725-a5e6ca2e7afe" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193149_135029_23667"/>
        <body>A ModelPropertyAssignment is an assignment of a ModelProperty to objects. &lt;example&gt;In the case of a welding operation, the welding points as a part of a wireframe model can be associated with a process operation to describe the locations where the robot has to weld for a welding process operation.&lt;/example&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1551194654787_913273_120125" xmi:uuid="8b4f97d5-7f49-4110-830c-e9db52c1f9b0" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_290014c_1550847743191_208266_98071"/>
        <body>These flowports are not bound to the ARM target because only a product definition property type can be assigned to it.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>ModelPropertyAssignment</name>
      <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193526_828085_25670" xmi:uuid="052204f2-309c-4f09-a638-e2ba81a2c281" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
