    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193042_855579_23449" xmi:uuid="7a1ade66-6d5f-4588-81ff-45155618a1a0" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_2_8e001ed_1457607917721_644762_43244" xmi:uuid="01621dab-e4a8-4d79-955b-1ab30b661fc9" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193042_855579_23449"/>
        <body>The classification information can be provided by several ways: &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt;by a simple class string; &lt;example&gt; A string 'company' specifies that an Organization is a company.&lt;/example&gt; &lt;note&gt;For the permissive list of values, this notion will be used.&lt;/note&gt;&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;by the definition of an explicit class; &lt;example&gt; A class with id 'company' classifies all Organization objects which are companies. The Class object allows for additional information like a description.&lt;/example&gt;&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;by the definition of an external class; &lt;example&gt; The information, that an Organization is classified as a company, is defined in an ExternalClass which is referenced by id and source.&lt;/example&gt;&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;by the definition of an external owl class. &lt;example&gt; The information, that an Organization is classified as a company, is defined in an ExternalOwlClass which is referenced by an URI.&lt;/example&gt;&lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>ClassSelect</name>
      <isAbstract>true</isAbstract>
    </packagedElement>
    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193306_841204_23948" xmi:uuid="7a2b8313-5c12-49d1-aa5d-e68504c911f3" xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType">
