      <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193979_394609_28571" xmi:uuid="7e5ff653-84c0-4d7b-84da-c1a8515329a5" xmi:type="uml:Property">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1455702134617_222521_42517" xmi:uuid="02e1404e-c7de-4dfe-a847-4240cc67f7c6" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193979_394609_28571"/>
          <body> the meaning of the relationship. Where applicable, the following class names shall be used: &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;'decomposition': The PropertyDefinitionRelationship defines a relationship where the Related PropertyDefinition is a member of a group of PropertyDefinition objects that is established by the Relating PropertyDefinition; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;'dependency': The related PropertyDefinition is dependent upon the Relating PropertyDefinition; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;'hierarchy': The business object defines a hierarchical relationship where the Related PropertyDefinitionn is on a lower level than the Relating PropertyDefinition; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;'peer': The related PropertyDefinition shall not be used without the Relating PropertyDefinitionn and vice versa; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;'substitution': The PropertyDefinitionRelationship defines a relationship where the Related PropertyDefinition replaces the Relating PropertyDefinition; &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;'value domain': The PropertyDefinitionRelationship defines a relationship where the values assigned to the Relating PropertyDefinition shall be within the limits indicated by the values assigned to the Related PropertyDefinition. &lt;example&gt; The output range of a 4-bit analog to digital converter is restricted to 16 discrete values, while the input voltage is restricted to a continuous range. &lt;/example&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</body>
        </ownedComment>
