    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193038_103118_23445" xmi:uuid="909353aa-ca3f-442e-a977-37ef19cce9c8" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1454496440606_352780_43098" xmi:uuid="e1c06783-fb16-45ff-b01d-68b70ee306c3" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193038_103118_23445"/>
        <body>A Class is a classification of an object which characterizes all objects of the same kind; such a classification is independent from the application of the classified object. &lt;example&gt; A fastener with subclasses, such as fastener with 2 or 3 fixture holes, a bracket with subclasses with 90 or 100 degrees bending angle, or screws with subclasses such as metal screws or machine screws are examples for Class. &lt;/example&gt;&lt;example&gt; For facilitating an effective part retrieval for slotted screws, several Class objects may be defined to classify screws:&lt;/example&gt; &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;A Class *1 with Description 'slotted screws' and three subclasses with the Descriptions *2: 'slotted cheese head screws - product grade A', *3: 'slotted pan head screws - product grade A', and *4: 'slotted countersunk flat head screws - product grade A'. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Each of the Class objects is based on a Class that further defines where the definition of the Class comes from. For Class *1 this is a company internal ExternalClassSystem for 'screw classes'. For the other Class objects these are ISO standardized ExternalClassSystem objects, namely for *2 'ISO 1207', for *3 'ISO 1580', and for *4 'ISO 2010'. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The Class objects may be characterized further by ClassAttribute objects. According to ISO 1207, the Class *2 has the attributes *11 with Id 'd' and Description 'thread', *12 with Id 'l' and Description 'nominal length', *13 with Id 'mechanical properties' and Description 'property class', etc. The possible values 'M1.6', 'M2', ..., 'M10' for ClassAttribute *11 may be defined as PropertyValue objects in a set of the attribute allowedValues. The according specification is given as &lt;a&gt;&lt;path&gt;./4_info_reqs_CommonResources.htm#PropertyValue.Name&lt;/path&gt; Name&lt;/a&gt; of the AO PropertyValue. The PropertyValue refer as their definition to a PropertyDefinition with the PropertyType 'nominal metric thread diameter'. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;To identify the designation 'Cheese head screw ISO 1207 - M5 x 20 x 4.8', a subclass of Class *2 is defined with the same Description 'slotted cheese head screws ISO 1207 -M5 x 20 x 4.8' but with the values for ClassAttribute corresponding to *11 restricted to 'M5' only, i.e., to get just the M5 screws, corresponding to *12 restricted to value '20' only, and corresponding to *13 restricted to value '4.8' only (for steel according to ISO 898-1). &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>Class</name>
      <ownedRule xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193461_670349_25250" xmi:uuid="8a9a15f0-7628-4d7c-a721-1a9c3e5ce0c1" xmi:type="uml:Constraint">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1721295759263_726027_151322" xmi:uuid="3575934f-fa56-4c74-becb-275390e83766" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1721295759264_841722_151323" xmi:uuid="9a150688-aabe-48ab-88c5-45cfba41b1d3" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <body> &lt;sch:rule context="//Class[@uid]"&gt; &lt;sch:let name="entity_name" value="if(@xsi:type) then substring-after(@xsi:type,':') else name()"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="uid" value="@uid"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="ids" value="child::Id/@id union child::Id/descendant::*[self::Identifier]/@id"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="followingAndPrecedingIds" value="following-sibling::Class/Id/@id union following-sibling::Class/Id/descendant::*[self::Identifier]/@id union preceding-sibling::Class/Id/@id union preceding-sibling::Class/Id/descendant::*[self::Identifier]/@id"/&gt; &lt;sch:assert test="count($ids) = 0 or not(some $i in $ids, $j in $followingAndPrecedingIds satisfies ($i eq $j))"&gt; The Id shall be unique. { -entity_name:&lt;sch:value-of select="$entity_name"/&gt; -entity_uid:&lt;sch:value-of select="$uid"/&gt; -rule_name:UR1 -attribute_name:Id -attribute_value:&lt;sch:value-of select="$ids"/&gt; } &lt;/sch:assert&gt; &lt;/sch:rule&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <body>Schematron</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_45e01bd_1513341822093_153812_93617" xmi:uuid="b7b8de29-4953-48d1-b6d7-6867e1727afe" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
