          <body> the set of Organization objects in that the Effectivity is valid. The value of this attribute need not be specified. If concernedOrganizations is an empty set, the Effectivity is globally applicable. &lt;example&gt;The Effectivity of the same part may be different in the various production sites of a car manufacturer. &lt;/example&gt;&lt;note&gt; As Effectivity is in most cases organization dependent, it is recommended always to populate the concernedOrganizations attribute.&lt;/note&gt; The value of this attribute need not be specified.</body>
