    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193062_774688_23498" xmi:uuid="9e0b939c-50fe-474d-9c32-71e4d3b7f13c" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1455726995976_117958_43192" xmi:uuid="a773bb86-efe7-46b1-9317-77269fed68bc" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193062_774688_23498"/>
        <body>A DateAndPersonAssignment is an object that associates a DateAndPersonOrganization with product data. This assignment provides additional information for the associated object. The provision of such data through this assignment has an organizational character whereas some objects require the same kind of data in order to be semantically complete. This assignment shall not be used to associate the corresponding organizational data with an object whose attributes are referencing the organizational data directly. &lt;example&gt; An example for the requirement stated is that there shall not exist a DateAndPersonAssignment with a role of 'requestor' that refers to a WorkRequest, since this object refers directly to DateAndPersonOrganization in that role. &lt;/example&gt;&lt;note&gt; In the context of the object DateAndPersonAssignment, the expression 'referenced object' means 'a concept that is conveyed within one of the instances referred to by the attribute assignedTo and not one of the instances referred to by this attribute. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;example&gt; If applied to an instance of Part with role 'creation', the DateAndPersonAssignment specifies the creation date of the part, tool, or raw material as a new object in the activity domain of the organization, and not the creation date of the instance of Part in the product management system of the organization. &lt;/example&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>DateAndPersonAssignment</name>
