      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1455702311113_84496_42526" xmi:uuid="4d5d5306-d826-4a38-bbc9-0a403f16dbb3" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193210_153036_23790"/>
        <body>A PropertyValue is the representation of PropertyDefinition by a numerical or textual value.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1515576081284_443506_265267" xmi:uuid="5d096047-51a5-4b11-a8e0-66342a492487" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <body>WR: encapsulated: SIZEOF(USEDIN(SELF,'')-(USEDIN(SELF, SCHEMA_NAME + 'PROPERTYVALUERELATIONSHIP.RELATING')+USEDIN(SELF, SCHEMA_NAME + 'PROPERTYVALUERELATIONSHIP.RELATED')))=1; Comment: there is no need of this OCL constraint because the SysML language intrinsically handles this concept of unicity of usage when the attribute is defined as PartProperty (in SysML, Aggregation as Composite in UML). PropertyValueRelationship Related and Relating attributes must be ReferenceProperty to ensure multiple usage of PropertyValue just in this case.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>PropertyValue</name>
