    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193067_889763_23512" xmi:uuid="ea98e02e-b8c5-4a4d-8775-11adb6cefcfc" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1515576316034_872151_265268" xmi:uuid="2342e554-113a-49c6-8aca-21f3513c81ea" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <body>WR: encapsulated: SIZEOF(USEDIN(SELF,''))=1; Comment: there is no need of this OCL constraint because the SysML language intrinsically handles this concept of unicity of usage when the attribute is defined as PartProperty (in SysML, Aggregation as Composite in UML). DescriptorRelationship Related and Relating attributes must be ReferenceProperty to ensure multiple usage of Descriptor just in this case.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1550054918218_357172_120188" xmi:uuid="39489557-a110-4474-bacf-74398fded1fd" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement href="../../../../SysML_ARM/SYSML_ARM_AP242.xmi#_2_attr_SYSML_ARM-Description_text_assignment-items"/>
        <body>Entities like Description_text_assignment, Classification_assignment, Identification_assignment, etc. have their items property unmapped in the mapping specification since they have to be completed where used.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1455732231723_845944_43277" xmi:uuid="ad0be6bc-4b27-4675-a361-10afba5ceb05" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193067_889763_23512"/>
        <body>A Descriptor is a set of words that describe something. &lt;example&gt;The same thing may have multiple descriptions associated with it. Assigning both a short description and a long description to an activity or an organization are examples of multiple descriptions applied to the same item. &lt;/example&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>Descriptor</name>
